Standalone data object definitions are data objects which are not part
of any other data object. They stand alone as definitions, in the same
way modules do. They also require naming, however, naming some of these
data objects only serves to cause aggravation for the user.

It is proposed to allow some data objects (determined by a flag) to not
require naming. Instead of the name delimitting the defintion, a symbol
or pair of symbols is used, such as square brackets.


